  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free in the ssl servername (SNI) callback\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19445.patch: take the SSLContext from the\n       connection and hold references to it and to the callback while the\n       callback runs, instead of using the borrowed pointer registered with\n       OpenSSL, and unregister the callback when the context is deallocated,\n       in Modules/_ssl.c, so a servername callback that switches the\n       connection to another context can no longer make the server call\n       through a freed SSLContext.\n     - CVE-2026-19445",
